      "author": "David A Case",
      "date_raw": "Fri, 5 Feb 2021 08:51:40 -0500",
      "body": "On Fri, Feb 05, 2021, Tomasz Miernik wrote:\n>During the calculations, I get an mdcrd file with the following content:\n>CDF^B^.^.^.^B^.^.^. .....\nLooks like what you should expect: the default trajectory format is netcdf,\nwhich is a binary format that you cannot edit. But other codes can read\nthis in, such as cpptraj, VMD, Chimera and others.\nIf you need to conver to an ASCII format, cpptraj can do that for you: set\ntrajin to your mdcrd file, and use \"trajout <filename>.crd\"\n...good luck...dac",
      "url": "http://archive.ambermd.org/202102/0047.html"
    },
