      "date_raw": "Sat, 6 Feb 2021 06:31:30 +0530",
      "body": "Hi\nThere seems to be no problem.\nWhat you tried to open in a text editor is netcdf (binary) format.\nI don’t see anything wrong in this unless you are unable to\nvisualize this in VMD or Chimera.\nOn Friday, 5 February 2021, Tomasz Miernik <\ntomasz.miernik.cm\n.\numk.pl> wrote:\n> Hello,\n> I'm using, Amber16, AmberTools17, Centos7,CUDA8.0/9.0/9.2.\n> Compilation looks good, .out file too:\n> -------------------------------------------------------\n> Amber 16 PMEMD 2016\n> -------------------------------------------------------\n>\n> | PMEMD implementation of SANDER, Release 16\n>\n> | Run on 11/18/2020 at 11:01:36\n>\n> | Executable path: /home/obliczenia/amber16/exe/pmemd.cuda\n> | Working directory: /home/zadania/miery/T_Amber\n> | Hostname: tesla4\n>\n> [-O]verwriting output\n>\n> File Assignments:\n> | MDIN: equil.in\n> | MDOUT: equil_1.out\n> | INPCRD: density.rst\n> | PARM: gsk3b_lig.prmtop\n> | RESTRT: equil_1.rst\n> | REFC: refc\n> | MDVEL: mdvel\n> | MDEN: mden\n> | MDCRD: equil_1.mdcrd\n> | MDINFO: mdinfo\n> | MDFRC: mdfrc\n>\n>\n> Here is the input file:\n>\n> equil com_4_sol\n> &cntrl\n> imin=0,irest=1,ntx=5,\n> nstlim=5000000,dt=0.002,\n> ntc=2,ntf=2,\n> cut=8.0, ntb=2, ntp=1, taup=2.0,\n> ntpr=500, ntwx=5000, ntwr=5000\n> ntt=3, gamma_ln=2.0,\n> temp0=300.0,\n> /\n> BUT\n> During the calculations, I get an mdcrd file with the following content:\n> CDF^B^.^.^.^B^.^.^.\n> ^.^.^.^F^.^.^.^Eframe^.^@^@^@^@^@^@^@^@^@^Gspatial^@^@^@^@^\n> C^.^.^.^Datom^.^.�h^@^@^@^Lcell_spatial^@^@^@^C^@^@^@^\n> Elabel^.^.^.^.^.^@^E^@^@^@^Lcell_angular^@^@^@^C^@^@^@^L^\n> .^.^.^F^.^.^.^Etitle^@^@^@^@^@^@^B^@^@^@^@^@^@^@^Kapplication^@^@^$\n> picosecond^@^@^@^@^@^E^@^@^@^D^@^@^@^@^@^@^C^\\^@^@^@^\n> Gspatial^@^@^@^@^A^@^@^@^A^@^@^@^@^@^@^@^@^@^@^@^B^@^@^@^D^@\n> ^.^.^.^.^.^C^D^.^.^.^Kcoordinates^.^.^.^.^C^.^.^.^.\n> ^@^@^@^B^@^@^@^A^@^@^@^L^@^@^@^A^@^@^@^Eunits^@^@^@^@^@^@^B^@^@^@^Hangst$\n> }B�A~BT�(B ��B�i%BP��B ��B�WmBM�tB\n> �EB��uBS��B^E`�B��*BU@�B^B��B